[0m[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  [0mWrote [0m[1m10[0m lines to [0m[1mnotes2.txt[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  1 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mRounding replaces a number with a nearby one that is easier to store.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  2 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mEvery finite format must round, because most real numbers need infinite digits.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  3 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mThe common rule is round half to even, also called banker's rounding.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  4 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mIt sends 2.5 to 2 and 3.5 to 4, so errors cancel instead of piling up.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  5 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mRound half up, taught in schools, drifts upward over many sums.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  6 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mIEEE 754 uses round to nearest even as its default mode.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  7 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mEach operation can add an error of at most half a unit in the last place.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  8 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mSmall errors compound when thousands of operations run in sequence.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m  9 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mSubtracting two near-equal numbers can wipe out most of the correct digits.[0m
     [0m[2m[38;2;248;248;242m 10 [0m[38;2;248;248;242mCareful code orders its sums to limit this loss, or rounds only once at the end.[0m

